15.4.1 梯度下降 (gradient descent) for both regression model but models like deep learning
> J(w,b) for linear regression or any functions 
> want min j(w,b), start with some w, b, like (w=0, b=0), then keeep changing w, b to reduce j(w,b) until we settle at or near a minumum
16.4.2 实现梯度下降
> w=w-α*∂J(w,b)/∂w, b=b-α*∂J(w,b)/∂b (α: learning rate, small positive number, if α is large, means to take big steps to take down hill, if α is small, means to take small steps to take down hill)
> ∂: derivative (导数), tell you which direction to take baby step and combine with learning rate α to take a step down hill to reduce J(w,b)
> in the graph of surface plot, repeat/update w, and b steps until convergence(收敛), meaning the steps are small enough to stop, and we have found the best w and b to make the model predict as accurately as possible
w=w-α*∂J(w,b)/∂w: 新的 w = 旧的 w − 一小步（w和b是同时更新的）
#∂J(w,b)/∂w=1/m*sum((fw,b(x)(i))-y(i))*x(i) (求导，对哪个求导，其余为常数) 
#∂J(w,b)/∂b=1/m*sum((fw,b(x)(i))-y(i)) (求导，对哪个求导，其余为常数)
17.4.3 梯度下降的直观理解
> learn more about what is learning rate and derivative 
> J(w,b), when b=0, w and cost function j is a two dimension graph （U-shape, 凸优化）: 
w=w-α*∂J(w)/∂w (导数J(w)/∂w 是cost function当前在某个点的切线斜率，告诉你在这个点上cost function的变化趋势，导数是正数，说明cost function在这个点上是上升的，想要下降，就要往负方向走，导数是负数，说明cost function在这个点上是下降的，想要下降，就要往正方向走)
18.4.4 学习率
> a: learning rate that is too small will take a long time to converge, a learning rate that is too large may overshoot the minimum and diverge, so we need to choose a proper learning rate to make the model converge to the minimum as fast as possible
> 在ununu型的cost function中，w=w-α*∂J(w)/∂w: 存在多个local minumum, 当梯度下降走到某个最低点时，导数会变成 0，因此它会停在那里，即使学习率等于0
