65.9.2 Softmax regression algorithm: generalization of logistic regression algorithm, to be able to carry out multiclass clssfication probem 
> it is a generalization of logistic regression, which is a binary classification algorithm to multi-cost classcification context 
> 
logistic regression: #two output values (1 or 0):
z=w.x+b, a=g(z)=1/(1+e^-z), a1=P(y=1|x), a2=P(y=0|x)=1-a1 #w, x here are vectors
softmax regression: # i.e., 4 possible output vales (1, 2, 3, 4):
z1=w1.x+b1, z2=w2.x+b2, z3=w3.x+b3, z4=w4.x+b4 
a1=g(z1)=e^z1/(e^z1+e^z2+e^z3+e^z4)=P(y=1|x) 
a2=g(z2)=e^z2/(e^z1+e^z2+e^z3+e^z4)=P(y=2|x) 
a3=g(z3)=e^z3/(e^z1+e^z2+e^z3+e^z4)=P(y=3|x)
a4=g(z4)=e^z4/(e^z1+e^z2+e^z3+e^z4)=P(y=4|x)
# a1+a2+a3+a4=1 
> general case （N possible outputs): y=1, 2, ....N：
zj=wj.x+bj, j=1, 2, ....N #w, x here are vectors
aj=e^zj/sum(e^zk)=P(Y=j|x) 
a1+a2+...+aN=1 
> how to specify cost function for softmax regression:
logistic regression: z=w.x+b, a1=g(z)=1/(1+e^-z)=P(y=1|x), a2=1-a1=P(y=0|x), loss=-ylog(a1)-(1-y)log(1-a1), J(w,b)=average loss 
softmax regression: a1=e^z1/(e^z1+e^z2+..+e^zN), ..., aN=e^zN/(e^z1+e^z2+...+e^zN), loss(a1, ....aN, Y)={-loga1 if y=1, -loga2 if y=2,.....-logaN if y=N}
if y=j, loss=-log(aj), the function is called crossentropy loss function, with a curve shape, as aj approaches 0, the loss L approach infinity, as aj approach 1, the loss L approac 0

