69.10.1 高级优化方法 (advanced optimization): train data faster than gradient descent
> wj=wj-alpha*∂/∂wj)*J(w,b) #w is a vector, alpha is learning rate 
when plot cost function J(w,b) as contour plot, the minumum of cost function is the center of the plot
if start the gradient descent from a point far away from the minimum, then it will take a long time to reach the minimum, because the gradient descent will take small steps to reach the minimum
Adam algorithm can help make learning rate adaptive, so that it can take larger steps when far away from the minimum, and smaller steps when close to the minimum, thus it can reach the minimum faster than gradient descent
> Adam algorithm: adaptive moment estimation, not just use single global learning rate alpha, also use different learning rate for every single parameter of model:
w1=w1-alpha1*∂/∂w1)*J(w,b) 
...
w10=w10-alpha10*∂/∂w10)*J(w,b)
b=b-alpha11*∂/∂b)*J(w,b)  
so here Adam algorithm can use 11 differen learning rates here 
if wj(or b) keep moving in same direction, increase alphaj
if wj(or b) keep oscillating back and forth, reduce alphaj 
>MNIST Adam 
