pick best w,b, report test error Jtest(w,b): 
>> bias and variance as a function of regularization parameter lambda: 
J(w,b)=(1/2m)*sum(fw,b(x^[i])-y^[i])^2+(lambda/2m)*sum(wj^2)
when lambda is 0, overfit, Jtrain low, Jcv high, high variance 
when lambda is too high, underfit, Jtrain high, Jcv high, high bias 
when lambda is just right, fit well, Jtrain low, Jcv low, just right bias and variance
Jtrain is a curve plot, as lambda increase, Jtrain increase
Jcv is a curve plot, as lambda increase, Jcv decrease first, then increase, when lambda is just right, Jcv is the lowest

