86.14.1 倾斜数据集的误差指标 (skewed dataset error metrics)
> if working on a ML application where ratio of positive and negative is very skewed, then accuracy is not a good metric to evaluate performance of your model, because it can be misleading
e.g., rare disease classification: 
tran classifer fw,b(x) (y=1 if diseae present, y=0 if disease absent)
supposed that youfind that you have got 1% error on test set (99% correct diagnoses) , 
but if only 0.5% of patients have the disease, then a classifier that always predicts y=0 (no disease) will have 99.5% accuracy, but it is not useful because it never detects the disease 
when dealing with skewed dataset, different error metric is recomended: precision/ recall 
>>precision: the number of true positive divided by the number classifeid as positive (number of predicted positive: true positive + false positive) #(e.g., of all patients where we predicted y=1, what fraction actually have the rare disease?)
>>recall: the number of true positive divided by the number of actual positives (number of actual positive: true positive + false negative) #(e.g., of all patients who actually have the rare disease, what fraction did we correctly identify?)
precision, 预测出来的结果，有多少是真的 (少误判，查准率)。recall, 真正应该找到的，有多少没有漏掉 （少漏判，查全率）。
>>y=1 in presence of rare diseaes we want to detect 
actual class: 1 or 0, predicted class 1 or 0
when actual class is 1, predicted class is 1: true positive (TP)
when actual class is 1, predicted class is 0: false negative (FN)
when actual class is 0, predicted class is 1: false positive (FP)
when actual class is 0, predicted class is 0: true negative (TN)

